; XENOGOLF MONO -- the title screen's palette, and nothing else's.
;
; It is PALETTE_ps1-soft.hex's own grey ramp with the hue taken out: each of the
; first 32 entries replaced by its Rec.709 luminance. So the tonal DISTRIBUTION
; is the one the rest of the game's look was built on -- dense in the shadows,
; even through the midtones -- and only the cast is gone. A fresh linear ramp
; would have been easy and would have banded differently in the darks, which is
; where this dither pass does its most visible work.
;
; WHY IT EXISTS. ps1-soft's greys go WARM above b0b0b0 (c0b8b0, e8d0d0, f8f0e8),
; so a white-on-black scene quantised through it comes back cream: the title's
; hologram measured rgb(192,184,176) -- a channel spread of 16 -- with 17% of
; the frame carrying visible chroma. On a screen whose whole brief is white on
; black that is the palette overruling the art.
;
; Every OTHER scene still uses LUT_ps1-soft. Its colours have somewhere to land
; in that palette and this one would flatten them to grey.
